{"skill":{"slug":"linkedin-automation","displayName":"LinkedIn Automation by Zich (BradAI's OpenClaw)"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1769856129853,"changelog":"Initial release: Automate LinkedIn content creation, posting, engagement, and analytics.\n\n- Post and schedule content (with optional images) directly to LinkedIn.\n- Track post analytics, audience growth, and engagement metrics.\n- Generate content ideas based on trending LinkedIn topics.\n- Automate liking and commenting on posts to boost engagement.\n- Includes strategies, workflows, and troubleshooting guides for effective LinkedIn automation.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2740,"sha256":"4a8ef164cc444e94d3fa297b2e2409546d93f51f283e9b4c81cba6a6a4fee5de","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/ideas.sh","size":1912,"sha256":"be81120f8fed803f431b4423b8d7cbb1d45c2977651dfda500eb60508b4882eb","contentType":"text/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/engage.sh","size":2185,"sha256":"aea278c0758ce58178f9d15793707cb3edadd42326e9f50153cbdf09fbc314c6","contentType":"text/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/schedule.sh","size":1435,"sha256":"0c59845987cf0df114a1c3f604ea12120d406734eccb5400e257788c4a370ea9","contentType":"text/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/analytics.sh","size":1453,"sha256":"173c973caa737df31d61fbab483d90fb014f77e358d96d54803830c71bedb605","contentType":"text/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/post.sh","size":1373,"sha256":"130467b15212aa036383f07b432096f8ff494c9a966e1a3e7cb6ab98b4bc569f","contentType":"text/x-sh"},{"path":"references/engagement.md","size":3416,"sha256":"b65fb8c329b2d15cb44cf7dbb07da472d5566d01aa2ad1eb5591f880ff3aae93","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/content-strategy.md","size":2787,"sha256":"808b145a960289357cb99897409a17109c8b512f14d1fb6efad2c3b070c8b827","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2359,"sha256":"a572b579c428518e46982490cdf49b985cdd46c55b8dcd25aab27a4337755fe6","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789024501765,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"62ae0069263d71123f80456475531ed22056d141cef25da2d7a4f705efd75884","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/62ae0069263d71123f80456475531ed22056d141cef25da2d7a4f705efd75884","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: linkedin-automation\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle is designed for LinkedIn automation, requiring the declared 'browser' tool. All scripts (`analytics.sh`, `engage.sh`, `ideas.sh`, `post.sh`, `schedule.sh`) output clear, explicit instructions for the AI agent to perform browser actions or schedule tasks using OpenClaw's native cron tool, directly aligning with the stated purpose. There is no evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, obfuscation, or prompt injection attempts to subvert the agent for harmful activities. The instructions are consistently within the expected scope of LinkedIn automation.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160414239},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":95,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":8,"checkedAt":1789024501765},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This LinkedIn skill is mostly a disclosed browser-workflow helper, but it can affect a real public account and its scheduled-post instructions are under-scoped and injection-prone.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Browser access to a logged-in LinkedIn session is proportionate for the stated purpose, but it is sensitive because the workflows can create public posts, public engagement, and access account analytics.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"I found no install hooks, dependency installation, remote payload retrieval, obfuscated code, or automatic local setup. The package is a SKILL.md file, reference markdown, and small shell scripts that print workflows.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The activation description is broad, and scripts/post.sh and scripts/schedule.sh mix user-supplied post content directly into operational agent instructions. schedule.sh also embeds content in a future main-session systemEvent without JSON serialization or a clear inert-data boundary.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill does not automatically create persistence, but schedule.sh instructs the user or agent to create an OpenClaw cron event targeting the main session, which could defer public account actions and preserve injected instruction text for later execution.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose matches LinkedIn posting, analytics, ideas, and engagement workflows, and the browser-with-LinkedIn-login requirement is disclosed. The concern is that the skill covers public posting, liking, commenting, analytics review, and growth tactics without strong per-action confirmation or reputation/privacy warnings.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable letting an agent work in a logged-in LinkedIn browser session. Review every generated post, comment, like, analytics request, and scheduled job before execution, and avoid using externally supplied post content without sanitizing it first. Be especially cautious with scheduled posts because the artifact suggests a main-session cron event that can run later with less immediate user oversight.","findings":"[TP4] expected: The scanner's mismatch concern is only partially supported: the scripts are workflow generators rather than direct LinkedIn API automation, but SKILL.md consistently frames the skill as browser-driven automation and provides selectors and workflows. This supports a scope/overstatement note, not a malicious finding.\n[P6] expected: Including post content in a posting workflow is expected, but the artifact does not separate user content from instructions, so crafted content could influence an agent operating a logged-in browser session.\n[SQP-1] unexpected: The broad description increases accidental activation risk for real LinkedIn account actions and lacks explicit constraints requiring exact user intent before posting, commenting, or analytics access.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: The public account action concerns are supported: posting, likes, comments, and engagement tracking are described, but the artifact mainly provides rate-limit advice rather than clear public-impact, privacy, or confirmation safeguards.\n[T01] expected: The static scan's instruction-injection concern is supported for post.sh and schedule.sh. This is not shell execution or credential theft, but it is material because the resulting text is meant to guide a privileged browser or future main-session agent.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789024501765}}}}}